  "title": "No value-free four-place law has mutual selection",
  "subject": "Whether any four-place law with no preferred value has recognisable failures on 4-regular systems and a hard count",
  "conclusion": "The 30 value-free four-place knots form four classes: parity's count is polynomial, not-exactly-two and twelve build equality without constants and are NP-complete on 4-regular systems, and not-all-equal never fails. So, unless NP-complete problems are polynomial, mutual selection among value-free laws is special to three places.",
